@*
    Where the interview stands, and what is still coming.

    The rail is the whole shape of the process and it is on the screen from the first question, lit
    at step one. An interview that shows only the question is a black box: the client cannot tell
    whether they are two minutes from the end or twenty, and the one thing every wizard owes them is
    the answer to that. So the five steps are always visible, and the four that have not been reached
    are dim rather than absent — words like *what it reaches for* mean little on the first screen,
    but a step nobody can see means less.

    Under it, the entries of the map appear as they are named, in the client's own words, and carry
    the second fact the rail cannot: steps two to five run once per entry, so which entry is under
    way is what says how far along the whole thing is.

    Neither part explains itself in prose. They are two kinds of thing — the shape of the work, and
    what the domain holds — and the eye tells them apart without being told.
*@

<div class="journey">

    <ol class="stations">
        @foreach ((string label, int index) in Steps.Select((step, index) => (step, index)))
        {
            <li class="station @Standing(index)">
                <span class="mark">@(index + 1)</span>
                <span class="name">@label</span>
            </li>
        }
    </ol>

    @if (Entries.Any())
    {
        <div class="domain">
            <span class="what">@Caption</span>

            <div class="kinds">
                @foreach ((IntentDraft intent, string standing) in Entries)
                {
                    <span class="@standing">@Named(intent)</span>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    }

</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The interview being reported on.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public InterviewState State { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// What the domain held before this interview, shown first and never lit.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public IEnumerable<IntentDraft> Established { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the agent in hand is finished and waiting for the client's word.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Written { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The whole interview, in the client's words: the map once, then four steps per entry of it.
    /// </summary>
    // The last is not a pass at all but the moment the client lets the agent into the domain, and it
    // is on the rail because from the outside it is simply the step where an entry is finished.
    private static readonly string[] Steps =
    [
        "what she takes care of",
        "what it is",
        "what it reaches for",
        "how it works",
        "into the domain"
    ];

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the map is still being drawn, in which case no entry is being written yet.
    /// </summary>
    private bool Drawing => State.Pass == InterviewPass.DomainMapper;

    /// <summary>
    /// What the strip of entries is, which changes once the map is closed and they start being
    /// worked through one at a time.
    /// </summary>
    private string Caption =>
        Drawing || State.At < 0
            ? "what your Morgana takes care of"
            : $"what your Morgana takes care of — writing {State.At + 1} of {State.Map.Count}";

    /// <summary>
    /// Every entry the client can see, with how it stands: what earlier sittings left, then today's
    /// map — written, being written, still ahead.
    /// </summary>
    private IEnumerable<(IntentDraft Intent, string Standing)> Entries =>
        Established.Select(i => (i, "already"))
            .Concat(State.Map.Select((intent, index) =>
                (intent, index < State.At ? "already" : index == State.At ? "under-way" : "ahead")));

    /// <summary>
    /// The client's own word for an entry: its button once it has one, its name until then.
    /// </summary>
    private static string Named(IntentDraft intent) => intent.Label ?? intent.Name ?? "…";

    /// <summary>
    /// Where the rail is lit.
    /// </summary>
    // The pass is the index by construction: the enum and this list are in the same order, the map
    // included. The last step is the exception — the interview stands there only once everything is
    // settled and the agent is waiting for the client's word.
    private string Standing(int index)
    {
        int here = Written ? Steps.Length - 1 : (int)State.Pass;

        return index == here ? "here" : index < here ? "done" : string.Empty;
    }
}
